problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set of products $$\mathcal{P}$$, a finite set of processes $$\mathcal{R}$$, and a weekly planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$.
- Each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ requires processing on the available processes, and the processing time per unit on process $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$ is given by $$a_{r,p}$$.
- Each process $$r$$ has a regular available weekly capacity $$C_{r,t}$$ in each period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- A designated process $$r^{\mathrm{O}}$$ allows overtime, with overtime availability $$O_{r,t}$$ in each period.
- Each product $$p$$ has a standard unit profit $$\pi_{p,t}$$.
- If a unit of product $$p$$ is completed using overtime on process $$r^{\mathrm{O}}$$, its realized profit is reduced by $$\delta_{p,t}$$.
- Each product has a minimum required production level $$L_{p,t}$$ in each period.
- A designated process $$r^{\mathrm{E}}$$ must be used exactly to its regular capacity in every period.
- The designated overtime-eligible process $$r^{\mathrm{O}}$$ should use its regular capacity fully, and any additional required time may be covered by overtime up to the overtime limit.
- The total realized profit over the planning horizon must meet or exceed the target $$\Pi^{\min}$$.
- Production quantities must be nonnegative, and unit counts are integer-valued whenever whole units are required.
- The optimization goal is to choose a weekly production plan and overtime allocation that satisfy the profit target, minimum production commitments, and process-utilization requirements while accounting for reduced profit on overtime production.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: total quantity of product $$p$$ produced in period $$t$$.
  - $$y_{p,t}$$: quantity of product $$p$$ whose work on process $$r^{\mathrm{O}}$$ is performed in overtime in period $$t$$.
  - $$h_t^{\mathrm{OT}}$$: overtime hours used on process $$r^{\mathrm{O}}$$ in period $$t$$.
  - $$d$$: optional deviation variables, if the model is built as a goal-attainment or priority-goal program.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "products": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$",
    "processes": "$$\\mathcal{R}$$",
    "periods": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$"
  },
  "parameters": {
    "processingTime": {
      "symbol": "$$a_{r,p}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "meaning": "hours required on process $$r$$ per unit of product $$p$$"
    },
    "regularCapacity": {
      "symbol": "$$C_{r,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "regular available hours on process $$r$$ in period $$t$$"
    },
    "overtimeCapacity": {
      "symbol": "$$O_{r,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "maximum overtime hours on process $$r$$ in period $$t$$"
    },
    "unitProfit": {
      "symbol": "$$\\pi_{p,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "standard profit per unit of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$"
    },
    "overtimeProfitReduction": {
      "symbol": "$$\\delta_{p,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "profit reduction per unit of product $$p$$ completed in overtime on $$r^{\\mathrm{O}}$$"
    },
    "minimumProduction": {
      "symbol": "$$L_{p,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "minimum required production of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$"
    },
    "profitTarget": {
      "symbol": "$$\\Pi^{\\min}$$",
      "meaning": "minimum total realized profit over the planning horizon"
    },
    "exactUtilizationProcess": {
      "symbol": "$$r^{\\mathrm{E}} \\in \\mathcal{R}$$",
      "meaning": "process that must be fully used exactly at its regular capacity"
    },
    "overtimeEligibleProcess": {
      "symbol": "$$r^{\\mathrm{O}} \\in \\mathcal{R}$$",
      "meaning": "process for which overtime is allowed"
    },
    "utilizationTargets": {
      "symbol": "$$U_{r,t}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "meaning": "target utilization hours for each process and period"
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "productionPlan": {
    "symbol": "$$x_{p,t}$$",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "total production quantity of each product in each period"
  },
  "overtimeAllocation": {
    "symbol": "$$y_{p,t}$$",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "quantity of each product whose designated overtime-process work is performed in overtime"
  },
  "overtimeUsage": {
    "symbol": "$$h_t^{\\mathrm{OT}}$$",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "overtime hours used on the overtime-eligible process in each period"
  },
  "goalDeviations": {
    "symbol": "$$d$$",
    "meaning": "optional deviation values for profit, production, and utilization targets if the chosen model uses goal programming"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "sets": {
    "products": ["$$A$$", "$$B$$"],
    "processes": ["$$I$$", "$$II$$"],
    "periods": ["$$\\tau_1$$"]
  },
  "parameters": {
    "processingTime": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6\\\\3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "regularCapacity": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}150\\\\70\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "overtimeCapacity": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}0\\\\30\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "unitProfit": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}300\\\\450\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "overtimeProfitReduction": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}20\\\\25\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "minimumProduction": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}10\\\\15\\end{bmatrix}$$",
    "profitTarget": "$$10000$$",
    "exactUtilizationProcess": "$$I$$",
    "overtimeEligibleProcess": "$$II$$",
    "utilizationTargets": "$$\\begin{bmatrix}150\\\\70\\end{bmatrix}$$"
  }
}
